-- A ledger read is not a function of its operands: `x is recorded as 7` is FALSE
-- before the RECORD and TRUE after it, in ONE evaluation of `top`, which is TRUE.
-- Keyed by its term alone, both reads were one atom, and `l4 verify` reported
-- `NOT A AND A`: unsatisfiable (found by adversarial review of
-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1013). Each occurrence of a leaf that reads the ledger, or calls
-- a rule that does, is now its own atom.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `x is recorded as` n IF (RECALL `x`) EQUALS JUST n

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `top` IF
        NOT `x is recorded as` 7
    AND (RECORD `x` IS 7) EQUALS 7
    AND `x is recorded as` 7

#EVAL `top`
